      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This review represents contemporary knowledge about pathogenetic aspects of evolvement and progress of human bronchial asthma. Main attention is given to cells and mediators of allergic inflammation, Th1/Th2-bias, remodeling of respiratory tract, genetic and exogenous risk markers. Moreover, opportunities and prospects for the use of laboratory animals in modeling bronchial asthma are assessed."},
